<!-- Added by Plutext Pty Ltd for the docx4j FO renderer (docx4j-fo-renderer), a modified distribution derived
     from Apache FOP 2.11: hook column-widths, a span="all" block after a column boundary (fop/CR-026 section 8). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      Columns of unequal width (265.65pt and 260.95pt with a 12pt gap on a 538.6pt body), seventy one-line blocks
      that overflow the first column, then a span="all" block and five more blocks. The restart at the column
      boundary used to make the span signal report a change on the first block read again, so the flow returned
      nothing and the page breaker opened a new two-column span on the page for every remaining block (thirty
      spans and as many body-overflow events on a corpus document). Now the first column holds 66 lines, the
      second the remaining 4, and the span="all" block follows: page 1 carries the columns' span and the empty
      span-all span, page 2 the block and the five after it (the columns before a span="all" block are not yet
      balanced for unequal widths, CR-026 phase B). The equal-columns control is laid the same way by Apache FOP.
    </p>
  </info>
  <fo>
    <fo:root xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fox="http://xmlgraphics.apache.org/fop/extensions"
        font-family="Helvetica" font-size="10pt" line-height="12pt">
      <fo:layout-master-set>
        <fo:simple-page-master master-name="p" page-width="595.3pt" page-height="841.9pt" margin-top="28.35pt" margin-bottom="14.2pt" margin-left="28.35pt" margin-right="28.35pt">
          <fo:region-body column-count="2" column-gap="12pt" fox:column-widths="265.65pt 260.95pt" fox:column-gaps="12pt"/>
        </fo:simple-page-master>
      </fo:layout-master-set>
      <fo:page-sequence master-reference="p">
        <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body">
      <fo:block>S1 short line</fo:block>
